WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t3-09-burnout-overload.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.040
You're still going.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.810
That's most of what there is to say about it today.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.910
And it is an accompaniment.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.600
It's just where you are.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:28.560
This practice isn't here to fix you and it asks very, very little of you.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.650
When you've been running on empty for a long time, your system doesn't crash
all at once.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.160
It fades out in stages.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.350
The momentum keeps you moving forward.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.870
But the sensation,

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.950
A part of you that actually feels connected to what you're doing

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.020
It goes offline first.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.840
That disconnect isn't a flaw.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.750
It's a circuit breaker.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:02.880
It's what happens when the demand has outpaced the supply for far too long.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:14.420
The next few minutes aren't about regaining your full capacity or getting back
to peak performance.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.840
They're just a quiet pause to let your system realize it doesn't have to push
for a moment.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.900
Four simple steps.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.560
You don't need to keep track or remember anything.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.220
I'll take you through

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.060
We'll start with something very small.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.710
Before we begin.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:43.990
Let's see.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.210
Can you wiggle your fingers?

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.240
Just a little.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:03.030
Press them gently into whatever is underneath you.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.110
Feel the surface holding your weight.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.450
That's done.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.900
Nothing bigger than that is required for a while.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.660
Let gravity have you for a moment.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.480
Step 1.

phase-recognise
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:27.940
Recognise

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.560
We will start by describing what you're feeling in just one word.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.760
Maybe that word is numb.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.560
Maybe it's drained

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.270
Empty or heavy

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.420
You don't need to locate where it sits in the body.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.010
That's often hard here, and not finding it is completely normal in this state.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.870
There is one thing worth knowing right now.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.400
This isn't ordinary tiredness.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.920
Tiredness lifts after a quiet weekend.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:18.410
This is what a nervous system does after a long time of putting out far more
than ever came in.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.740
The flatness is what's left when there is nothing spare.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.730
It does not respond to being pushed through.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.060
And you've likely tested that already.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.630
Step 2

phase-regulate
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.020
Regulate

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.830
This step is not about calming down.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.180
Feeling flat is not too much feeling.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.160
An easy, even breath.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.050
Close to your normal pace.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.340
And warmth at your chest.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.080
That is what reaches you right now.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.100
Contact first

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.710
Counting can wait

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:18.180
Place a hand over your chest or hold your own arm, whichever is nearer.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.000
Let it stay there.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.680
Let the warmth of your skin transfer through.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.120
Now the breath

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.750
And it doesn't need to be counted today.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.780
Just an even breath.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:36.860
Both ways.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.450
That's all this step needs.

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.370
Breathing in.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.280
And breathing out.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.720
There is nothing to achieve here.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.410
Nobody is checking.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.170
Thoughts may come

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.430
They may not.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.720
Either one is fine here.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.150
If a thought comes, you don't have to do anything with it.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.790
Let it sit there

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.740
You are the one noticing the thought

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.640
You are not the one who has to answer it.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.990
Whether passes through a room

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.600
The room doesn't become the weather.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.790
You are the room.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.290
Step three.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.250
There are two separate things going on right now.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.310
And only one of them is the actual load.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.270
First, there is what's actually being asked of you.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:46.880
It is real

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.820
Probably unreasonable and largely not yours to fix from a chair.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.390
And then,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.340
There is the pushing through.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.700
Carrying on as though the tank weren't empty.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:09.180
Adding the effort of appearing fine to the heavy effort of the work itself.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:14.900
Getting up tomorrow and doing it again on the assumption that stopping isn't
available.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.510
That second part costs more than the work does.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.610
And it is the only one of the two you can put down right now.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.580
Putting it down isn't the same as quitting.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.200
Nobody here is telling you to stop.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:31.730
Only you know what stopping would cost you.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.720
Just acknowledge that pretending is a second job.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.330
And it's the one that isn't paying

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.530
And notice the question running in the background.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.310
"What's wrong with me that I can't cope with this?"

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.840
Put that question down too

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:07.320
The load may be genuinely beyond what one person can carry.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.440
That question puts the fault in the wrong place entirely.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.130
Instead, ask gently.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.140
What was this for?

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.860
Something in you kept absorbing

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.080
Every time there was more, it went to you.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.660
And each time you found somewhere to put it

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.060
That is a capability.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.650
And it's why the volume kept arriving.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.590
Reliable people get given more.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.720
That's not a moral failing.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.190
It's just what happens

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.840
You don't need the answer right now.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.520
Keep the question

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.410
It's worth coming back to when you're steadier.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.280
Some of this weight belongs to today.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.220
Some of it may be older.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.260
You don't have to sort out which is which yet.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.030
Just notice there might be both

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:06.920
Step 4.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.320
Rise

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.590
Picture yourself from across the room right now.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.660
Hand on your chest, still going.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.290
You're not failing at this.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.260
You are simply out of fuel.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.910
Now picture a version of yourself that you'd want to be on a day like this.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.040
Not a grand plan.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:51.470
Just choosing one small thing that puts a little bit back.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.810
Eating a real meal today.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.740
Leaving on time.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.070
Not opening your laptop after dinner.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.650
Going to bed early.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:10.180
It sounds small against the sheer size of the overload.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:15.860
But it's still what's on offer, and nothing else works until some of your
energy comes back.
